u^{
u}(t)=e^{
u \Delta t}u_0 - \int_0^t 	ext{div}(e^{
u\Delta (t-s)}
\mathbb{P}(u^{
u}(s)\otimes u^{
u}(s))) \,ds \quad 	ext{ for all } t\in [0,T),$$
where $e^{
u\Delta t}$ is the heat semigroup defined via the Fourier multiplier $e^{-4\pi^2
